.TH DANBY-AEROBRAKING 1
.SH NAME
danby-aerobraking \- orbital energy loss during atmospheric passes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/aerobraking
.SH MODEL
Central gravity produces the orbit while exponential atmosphere applies drag
near planetary radius. Repeated periapsis passages lower speed and apoapsis.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/aerobraking.b
.PP
Its
.B rhs()
is written as literal
.IR eqn (7)
strings (see
.IR eqn2hoc (2)),
not hand-coded Limbo arithmetic - both the central-gravity and
atmospheric-drag terms, tied directly to the
.IR orbital (2)
interface with no separate
.B Atmosphere
module call. See
.IR aerobrakingtest (1).
